# N3 example: derivative.
# Companion to derivative.eye/.srl: symbolic differentiation over
# constructor terms, here represented as N3 lists (:const N), (:var X),
# (:add U V), (:mul U V) matched structurally by each backward rule's own
# head pattern (mirroring hanoi.n3's (?N ?X ?Y ?Z) style), since
# constructing a blank-node property bag in a backward (<=) rule's
# conclusion was found not to work (confirmed by testing in isolation).

@prefix log: <http://www.w3.org/2000/10/swap/log#>.
@prefix : <https://eyereasoner.github.io/eyepl/examples/derivative#>.

{((:const ?n) ?x) :derivative (:const 0)} <= true.
{((:var ?x) ?x) :derivative (:const 1)} <= true.
{((:var ?y) ?x) :derivative (:const 0)} <= {?y log:notEqualTo ?x}.

{((:add ?u ?v) ?x) :derivative (:add ?du ?dv)} <= {
    (?u ?x) :derivative ?du.
    (?v ?x) :derivative ?dv.
}.

{((:mul ?u ?v) ?x) :derivative (:add (:mul ?du ?v) (:mul ?u ?dv))} <= {
    (?u ?x) :derivative ?du.
    (?v ?x) :derivative ?dv.
}.

{((:mul (:var :x) (:var :x)) :x) :derivative ?d} => {:query :derivative ?d}.
